{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-44312",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $c,$ so we will treat the other variables $a$ and $b$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $c.$\n\nFirst, we add $2c$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6a & =9b-2c \\\\ -6a+2c & =9b-2c+2c \\\\ -6a+2c & =9b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $6a$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6a+2c & =9b \\\\ -6a+2c+6a & =9b+6a \\\\ 2c & =9b+6a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c & =9b+6a \\\\ \\frac{2c}{2} & =\\frac{9b+6a}{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{9b+6a}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
